.venv
.claude
.devcontainer
__pycache__
nul
*.csv
*.pdf
*.md
pdf_converter.py
test_backend.py

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Named explicitly rather than relying on a blanket `*.json`. The repo is
# PUBLIC, so this list is the last line of defence — add to it, never remove.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
# GCP service-account keys arrive under many names, so match loosely rather
# than listing the ones seen so far. A missed pattern here is a leaked key.
key.json
**/key.json
*key*.json
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*-sa.json
*sa-*.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
*.pfx
*.jks

# Written at runtime by the Phone Connect and Email Import pages. Holds a Gmail
# APP PASSWORD plus the Telegram and Discord bot tokens — it is a secrets file
# that happens to be named like config, and it lives in the repo root.
.bot_config.json
**/.bot_config.json

# ── User finance data (privacy, not secrecy) ─────────────────────────────────
# These hold real expense/income records. Never commit them.
data.json
rules.json
**/data.json
backups/

# Generated exports. export_to_csv / export_to_pdf / the Monthly Summary page
# all write these into whatever directory the app was started from, which is
# normally the repo root. *.csv and *.pdf are ignored wholesale above; these are
# named too so the intent survives if those broad rules are ever narrowed.
expenses.csv
income.csv
subscriptions.csv
monthly_summary.pdf
expenses*.pdf
income*.pdf

# Somewhere to drop receipt images without them landing in a public repo.
receipts/

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.streamlit/secrets.toml
licenses.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Node / web ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
web/dist/
.vercel

# NOTE: `*.json` used to be ignored wholesale. That also excluded
# web/package.json, web/package-lock.json and web/vercel.json — without which
# the Vercel build of web/ cannot run at all — while giving only incidental
# cover to the real secrets, which are now listed above by name.

# Internal working notes. NOT for the public repo — it maps the GCP project,
# the exact deploy commands, which Secret Manager entries exist and what the
# admin endpoints are. No secret values, but it is reconnaissance material.
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
